# 17. Security and Secret Handling

Verify:

- Authentication
- Authorization
- Capabilities
- ACL
- Runtime mode
- Kill Switch
- Provider connection
- Secret handling
- Logging redaction
- Audit history
- External side effects
- Failure behavior

Never expose:

- JWTs
- Tokens
- API keys
- API Secrets
- Credentials
- Encryption payloads
- Chat IDs
- Authorization headers
- Authenticated WebSocket URLs
- Raw environment files
- Sensitive provider payloads
- Signed provider queries

Every sensitive failure must fail closed.

## Canonical Credential Rule

Provider credentials must have one canonical encrypted server-side owner.

Do not store provider Secrets in:

- localStorage
- IndexedDB
- frontend state beyond transient input
- URLs
- logs
- audit metadata
- metrics labels

Stored credentials must not be prefilled into forms.

Credential rotation must use new transient values.

Delete and disable actions must require confirmation.

