# 18. Official Provider Documentation Rule

Provider-specific facts must come from official provider documentation.

Use official sources for:

- Endpoints
- Signing
- Headers
- Timestamp
- Receive window
- Permission semantics
- Rate limits
- Error codes
- Maintenance behavior
- Network requirements
- Deposit/withdrawal rules
- Futures rules
- P2P rules
- Account-edit rules

Record:

- Exact official pages used
- Retrieval date
- Selected endpoints
- Permission requirements
- Known provider limitations

Do not rely on blogs, forums or copied examples as the primary contract.

Do not include real credentials or signed requests in documentation.

